  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feed the Future Zimbabwe-Fostering Agribusiness for Resilient Markets (FTFZ-FARM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Zimbabwe):  The Feed the Future Zimbabwe Fostering Agribusiness for Resilient Markets (FARM) activity will promote water harvesting techniques to smallholder farmers, encourage them to invest in water supply and to adopt conservation practices by constructing boreholes, deep wells, drip irrigation systems, and water basins. It will also help farmers to prepare for the La Nina season by investing in water harvesting and storage facilities. This aims at reducing the negative impact of frequent drought and prolonged dry spells on farm production and productivity. The activity will intensify private sector engagement to increase access to quality agricultural inputs, and strengthen markets for agricultural produce. It will also promote access to formal and informal finance that will enable farmers to invest in water supply and other on-farm and off-farm activities. The activity promotes the adoption of improved seed varieties to mitigate the effects of climate change, improve post-harvest  handling to reduce losses; provide training on improved agricultural production and post-harvest handling practices; and business skills. It will also facilitate improved adoption of household nutrition status and hygiene. More than 60 percent of activity beneficiaries are women. Therefore, the successful implementation of activity implementations will increase women&apos;s financial contributions to their households, resulting in improving their status in their communities and contributing to reducing gender-based violence. The activity is working closely with other USAID Economic Growth and Humanitarian Assistance and Resilience activities to maximize USAID development investments by leveraging resources.</narrative>
  </description>
